# Workspace install layout.
#
# The example apps (examples/expo, examples/bare) are bundled by Metro, which
# resolves a package's TRANSITIVE deps from the app's own node_modules. pnpm's
# default strict (symlinked, non-flat) layout hides expo's / react-native's own
# deps (expo-constants, expo-file-system, expo-font, …) from Metro, so bundling
# fails with "Unable to resolve …". `node-linker=hoisted` flattens node_modules
# (npm/yarn-style) so Metro can resolve them. This is Expo's documented fix for
# pnpm monorepos. pnpm applies this workspace-wide (not per-package).
#
# This affects only the local install layout — NOT the published package, whose
# contents are controlled by `files: ["dist", …]` in package.json.
node-linker=hoisted
